1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:08,170
On a cold, damp evening in mid-November, a sharp wind cut through the streets, but Jack paid little attention to the chill.
十一月中旬一个阴冷潮湿的傍晚，凛冽的寒风穿街而过，杰克却没怎么在意这股寒意。

2
00:00:08,970 --> 00:00:17,630
As a delivery rider, he had just finished a few smooth orders, his hands warm from the hot milk tea cups he’d been carrying, and his spirits fairly good.
身为外卖骑手，他刚刚顺利送完几单，一直端着的热奶茶杯把他的双手焐得暖暖的，心情也相当不错。

3
00:00:18,430 --> 00:00:24,730
Stepping out of a milk tea shop, he found the spot where his second-hand electric bike had been parked now empty.
一走出奶茶店，他就发现停放那辆二手电动车的地方空了。

4
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:32,370
In an instant, his heart sank, and a wave of hopelessness swept over him, turning his calm evening into a nightmare.
刹那间，他的心一沉，一股绝望涌上心头，平静的傍晚变成了一场噩梦。

5
00:00:33,170 --> 00:00:41,330
That bike was far more than just a vehicle; it was his lifeline, the only way for him to earn daily income and cover his living expenses.
那辆电动车远不只是一个交通工具，它是他的命根子，是他挣取日常收入、支付生活开销的唯一途径。

6
00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:49,430
Panic set in as he remembered the undelivered orders—especially a cup of hot milk tea for Ms. White, a regular customer.
他想起那些还没送出的订单，顿时慌了神——尤其是给老顾客怀特女士的那杯热奶茶。

7
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:59,550
His hand trembled as he pressed the voice button, his words laced with sorrow and anxiety as he apologized repeatedly, offering to pay for the undelivered drink.
他按下语音键时手在发抖，话语里满是愧疚和焦虑，他一遍遍地道歉，主动提出赔付那杯没送到的饮料。

8
00:01:00,350 --> 00:01:06,240
To his great surprise, Ms. White did not respond with anger or complaint, but with gentle kindness.
让他大感意外的是，怀特女士没有生气，也没有抱怨，而是温和友善地回应了他。

9
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:10,920
Ms. White told him not to worry and to take his time finding his bike.
怀特女士让他别着急，慢慢找车。

10
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:16,360
Her understanding words calmed him but also deepened his sense of responsibility.
她体谅的话语让他平静下来，却也让他的责任感更强了。

11
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,200
“She is so kind.
“她人真好。

12
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:20,550
I cannot let her down,” he thought.
我不能辜负她。”他心想。

13
00:01:21,350 --> 00:01:26,530
For nearly two hours, he searched every nearby street, but there was no sign of his bike.
他在附近的每条街上找了将近两个小时，却始终不见车子的踪影。

14
00:01:27,330 --> 00:01:32,560
As night grew darker and the wind bit harder, Jack clenched his fists and made a firm decision.
夜色越来越深，寒风也越刮越刺骨，杰克握紧双拳，下定了决心。

15
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:42,950
He took out his meager savings, bought a bag of fresh apples and a new cup of hot milk tea, then set off on foot to Ms. White’s apartment, several kilometers away.
他拿出自己微薄的积蓄，买了一袋新鲜苹果和一杯新的热奶茶，然后步行前往几公里外怀特女士的公寓。

16
00:01:43,750 --> 00:01:55,350
The wind bit into his thin jacket, and his old shoes grew heavy with mud, but the thought of keeping his promise and maintaining his integrity kept him moving forward through the dimly lit urban landscape.
寒风钻进他单薄的夹克，旧鞋沾满泥巴、越走越沉，可一想到要信守承诺、守住自己的诚信，他就在昏暗的城市街景中一路向前走去。

17
00:01:56,150 --> 00:02:00,080
Finally, breathless, Jack reached Ms. White’s doorstep and rang the bell.
终于，杰克气喘吁吁地来到怀特女士家门口，按响了门铃。

18
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:05,850
Deeply moved by Jack’s action, Ms. White decided to share the story online that night.
杰克的举动深深打动了怀特女士，她决定当晚把这个故事发到网上。
